<h1>New Construction Builders in San Antonio 2026</h1>

<p>For military families considering new construction homes in San Antonio, navigating the dozens of active builders and their various communities can feel overwhelming. Each builder offers distinct floor plans, price points, amenities, and warranty programs. Understanding the major builders, their communities, and their reputations helps military families identify which builders align with their needs and budget.</p>

<p>This comprehensive guide profiles San Antonio's leading homebuilders serving the military market, helping you make informed decisions about new construction options.</p>

<h2>Why Choose New Construction?</h2>

<p>Before exploring builders, understand why military families often choose new construction. Modern systems provide energy efficiency and lower utility costs. Warranties protect against defects. Customization options allow tailoring homes to specific preferences. And for military families living through frequent moves, new homes offer fresh starts and modern living spaces.</p>

<p>However, new construction comes with trade-offs: premium pricing, construction timeline uncertainty, and reliance on builder quality and responsiveness. Choosing the right builder mitigates these concerns and ensures positive experiences.</p>

<h2>Major San Antonio Builders Serving Military Markets</h2>

<h3>Toll Brothers</h3>

<p>Toll Brothers is one of the nation's largest luxury homebuilders, operating communities throughout North San Antonio. Known for premium homes and sophisticated designs, Toll Brothers serves military families with higher budgets seeking prestige locations like The Dominion in Spring Branch.</p>

<p><strong>Strengths:</strong> Premium homes with high-end finishes, established reputation for quality, strong warranty programs, luxury amenities in communities</p>

<p><strong>Considerations:</strong> Significantly higher prices ($500,000+), smaller lot sizes in many communities, higher HOA fees</p>

<p><strong>Military Appeal:</strong> Officers and higher-ranking military families appreciate Toll Brothers' prestige and amenities. The Dominion location provides proximity to higher-ranking military officers and strong community presence.</p>

<h3>Beazer Homes</h3>

<p>Beazer Homes operates multiple communities throughout San Antonio with diverse floor plans and price points. Known for customer service and community amenities, Beazer builds across North San Antonio suburbs serving various budgets.</p>

<p><strong>Strengths:</strong> Diverse floor plans and price points, strong customer service focus, modern designs, reasonable pricing</p>

<p><strong>Considerations:</strong> Quality varies by community, some communities experience slower appreciation, less prestige than some competitors</p>

<p><strong>Military Appeal:</strong> Beazer's focus on customer service and reasonable pricing appeals to middle-rank military families. Several Beazer communities have significant military populations.</p>

<h3>Meritage Homes</h3>

<p>Meritage operates multiple North San Antonio communities with energy-efficient homes and customer-centric floor plans. Known for customization options and warranty coverage, Meritage serves budget-conscious families seeking modern homes.</p>

<p><strong>Strengths:</strong> Energy-efficient homes reducing utility costs, extensive customization options, warranty protection, reasonable pricing</p>

<p><strong>Considerations:</strong> Smaller communities in some areas, less luxury finishing than premium builders, some locations farther from San Antonio center</p>

<p><strong>Military Appeal:</strong> Military families appreciate Meritage's energy efficiency reducing monthly costs and customization allowing personalization within budget constraints.</p>

<h3>David Weekley Homes</h3>

<p>David Weekley is known for personalized service and design-forward homes. Operating premium communities throughout North San Antonio, Weekley builds sophisticated homes appealing to discerning military families.</p>

<p><strong>Strengths:</strong> Premium designs and finishes, personalized buyer experience, strong warranty, sophisticated floor plans</p>

<p><strong>Considerations:</strong> Higher pricing, longer construction timelines, more selective about buyer financing</p>

<p><strong>Military Appeal:</strong> Officers valuing design quality and personalized service appreciate Weekley's approach. However, military families on tight timelines may find construction delays problematic.</p>

<h3>Lennar Homes</h3>

<p>Lennar is one of the nation's largest builders with multiple San Antonio communities. Known for diverse price points and extensive warranty offerings, Lennar serves military families across the rank spectrum with varied budgets.</p>

<p><strong>Strengths:</strong> Broad price range, excellent warranty programs, multiple community options, strong builder support</p>

<p><strong>Considerations:</strong> Quality and finishes vary by community, less prestige than some competitors, mixed military family experiences</p>

<p><strong>Military Appeal:</strong> Lennar's broad range and strong warranties appeal to military families seeking affordability combined with protection. Multiple communities provide location flexibility.</p>

<h3>Pulte Homes</h3>

<p>Pulte operates communities throughout North San Antonio with diverse floor plans and price points. Known for reliability and customer service, Pulte builds homes serving military families with moderate budgets.</p>

<p><strong>Strengths:</strong> Established reputation, diverse communities, reasonable pricing, good warranty programs</p>

<p><strong>Considerations:</strong> Less distinctive than some competitors, communities may feel less exclusive, finishing quality varies</p>

<p><strong>Military Appeal:</strong> Military families value Pulte's reliability and established reputation. Multiple communities provide options throughout North San Antonio.</p>

<h3>Ashton Woods Homes</h3>

<p>Ashton Woods operates communities in Bulverde and North San Antonio suburbs with mid-to-premium pricing. Known for open floor plans and customer-responsive designs, Ashton Woods serves military families seeking balance between quality and value.</p>

<p><strong>Strengths:</strong> Open floor plans popular with modern families, customer-responsive design, good value positioning, solid warranty</p>

<p><strong>Considerations:</strong> Smaller builder with less national presence, fewer community options than major builders, less luxury finishing</p>

<p><strong>Military Appeal:</strong> Military families appreciate Ashton Woods' focus on functional design and reasonable pricing. Bulverde communities appeal to families seeking rural character.</p>

<h2>Comparing Builders: Key Criteria</h2>

<h3>Price Range and Budget Alignment</h3>

<p>Builders operate across distinct price ranges. Toll Brothers and Weekley command $500,000+. Beazer, Meritage, Lennar, and Pulte operate in the $300,000-$450,000 range. Ashton Woods and regional builders fill niche price points. Match your budget to appropriate builders to avoid wasting time on unaffordable options.</p>

<h3>Warranty Coverage</h3>

<p>Warranties vary significantly. Most major builders offer 1-year, 5-year, and 10-year warranties covering structural, system, and cosmetic defects. Compare warranty terms carefully—some builders offer more comprehensive coverage or longer protection periods.</p>

<p>David Weekley, Meritage, and Lennar are known for strong warranty programs. Ask about specific coverage and claims processes before committing.</p>

<h3>Customization and Design Options</h3>

<p>Some builders offer extensive customization, allowing floor plan modifications and premium finishes. Others offer limited options with defined packages. Military families preferring personalized homes should prioritize builders offering customization.</p>

<p>David Weekley and Meritage offer strong customization. Toll Brothers offers limited customization but distinctive premium designs.</p>

<h3>Construction Timeline Reliability</h3>

<p>Military families on strict timelines need builders known for meeting construction deadlines. Ask potential builders for references from other military families about construction timeline reliability. Some builders consistently deliver on schedule; others frequently miss target dates.</p>

<p>Larger builders (Lennar, Pulte, Beazer) have better track records meeting timelines than smaller builders. However, individual experiences vary by community.</p>

<h3>Community Amenities and Lifestyle</h3>

<p>Builders vary in community amenities. Toll Brothers operates resort-style communities with championship golf courses. Meritage focuses on efficient, family-oriented communities. Ashton Woods emphasizes open spaces and outdoor living. Match your lifestyle preferences to builder strengths.</p>

<h2>San Antonio Builder Communities Worth Exploring</h2>

<h3>Spring Branch Area Communities</h3>

<p><strong>The Dominion (Toll Brothers):</strong> Premier luxury gated community with championship golf course, resort amenities, and prestigious address. Homes $500,000+. Appeals to high-ranking officers seeking prestige.</p>

<p><strong>Spring Branch Heights (Beazer/Meritage):</strong> Mid-range communities with modern homes $300,000-$400,000. Strong schools and community amenities. Appeals to families seeking quality and value.</p>

<h3>Schertz/Cibolo Communities</h3>

<p><strong>Sonterra (Toll Brothers):</strong> Master-planned community with diverse builders, premium amenities, and reasonable proximity to Lackland. Homes $300,000-$500,000.</p>

<p><strong>Cross Creek (Meritage/Lennar):</strong> Family-oriented community with modern homes, parks, and amenities. Homes $280,000-$400,000. Appeals to active-duty families with military budgets.</p>

<h3>Bulverde Communities</h3>

<p><strong>Scenic Vista (Ashton Woods):</strong> Rural-character community with larger lots and open spaces. Mid-range pricing $300,000-$400,000. Appeals to families seeking country lifestyle.</p>

<h2>Builder Red Flags and Concerns</h2>

<p>When evaluating builders, watch for these warning signs:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Excessive Change Order Costs:</strong> Builders nickeling-and-diming for upgrades suggest predatory practices</li>
<li><strong>Poor Customer Reviews:</strong> Consistently negative feedback on warranty claims, customer service, or timeline reliability</li>
<li><strong>Financial Instability:</strong> Bankrupt or distressed builders risk leaving homes unfinished</li>
<li><strong>Limited Transparency:</strong> Builders reluctant to provide references, warranty details, or pricing breakdowns</li>
<li><strong>Aggressive Sales Tactics:</strong> Pressure to commit before understanding terms or exploring alternatives</li>
<li><strong>Multiple Builder Complaints:</strong> Texas Real Estate Commission (TREC) complaints indicate systemic problems</li>
</ul>

<h2>Vetting Builders: Due Diligence Steps</h2>

<h3>Request References</h3>

<p>Ask builders for references from recent military clients. Call references and ask specifically about:</p>

<ul>
<li>Timeline reliability—did construction meet promised dates?</li>
<li>Quality—any defects or issues discovered?</li>
<li>Warranty service—responsive and helpful with claims?</li>
<li>Sales experience—transparent, respectful, pressure-free?</li>
<li>Overall satisfaction—would they buy from this builder again?</li>
</ul>

<h3>Review TREC Complaints</h3>

<p>Check Texas Real Estate Commission (TREC) complaint history for builders. While isolated complaints are normal, patterns of complaints indicate problems. TREC maintains public complaint databases searchable by builder.</p>

<h3>Tour Model Homes and Communities</h3>

<p>Visit model homes and communities in person. Evaluate construction quality, finishes, floor plan functionality, and community amenities. Talk with residents currently living in builder communities to learn about actual experiences.</p>

<h3>Understand Pricing and Upgrades</h3>

<p>Request detailed pricing showing base price, available upgrades, and typical upgrade costs. Some builders show low base prices but push costly upgrades. Transparency about upgrade costs helps you budget accurately.</p>

<h2>Military Family Considerations When Choosing Builders</h2>

<h3>Warranty Importance</h3>

<p>Military families relocating frequently cannot easily address warranty claims from distance. Choose builders known for responsive warranty service and clear claims processes. Meritage, Lennar, and Weekley have strong reputations for warranty responsiveness.</p>

<h3>Relocation and Lease-Back Options</h3>

<p>Ask builders about possession timing flexibility. Can you close early and lease from the builder until construction completes? Can you lease the home back to the builder briefly after closing? These options help manage military family transitions.</p>

<h3>Timeline Clarity</h3>

<p>Ensure you understand actual construction timelines with buffer for delays. Don't allow tight timelines to force you into homes with quality concerns or problematic builders. Your PCS flexibility matters more than perfect timing.</p>

<h2>Action Steps for Builder Selection</h2>

<ol>
<li>Determine your budget and identify builders in your price range</li>
<li>Visit 3-5 builder model homes and communities</li>
<li>Request references from recent military clients</li>
<li>Call references and ask detailed questions about experiences</li>
<li>Review TREC complaint history for builders you're considering</li>
<li>Request detailed pricing and upgrade information</li>
<li>Compare warranty offerings across builders</li>
<li>Evaluate community amenities and lifestyle alignment</li>
<li>Make selection based on overall value, not just price</li>
</ol>

<h2>Conclusion</h2>

<p>San Antonio has numerous quality builders serving military families at various price points. Success comes from thorough vetting, understanding builder differences, and matching your priorities to builder strengths. The cheapest builder isn't necessarily the best value if warranty service is poor or construction quality is questionable.</p>

<p>Take time evaluating builders, gathering references, and understanding what you're purchasing. The builder you choose impacts your home's quality, your building experience, and your long-term satisfaction. Choose carefully and you'll enjoy your new San Antonio home throughout your military assignment.</p>

